IMPORT prelude

-- Financial Procedure Act 1966 (Singapore) -- the controls on public money that have decision content: the financial year (s 2),
-- the two Consolidated Fund accounts (s 6), bank accounts and overdrafts (s 4), what public money may be invested in (s 7), capital
-- injections (s 7A), Contingencies Fund advances (s 11), warrants to issue money from the Consolidated Fund (s 12(3)), when a
-- guarantee or loan binds Singapore (s 15), virement between subheads (s 17(4)), transfer of functions between heads (s 17A),
-- and surcharge of public servants for losses (ss 20 to 23). The Accountant-General's protected terms (s 2A(2)) are included.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FPA1966.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 3 of 2024 (in force 26 February 2024) shown. The Schedule (moneys to be invested on deposit in a bank, s 7(7)) is EMPTY in
-- the deposit: it has a title and no entries.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 32 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the provisions above. Not encoded: the
-- Accountant-General's duties (s 2B), accounting officers' general duty (s 3), the Minister's general powers (s 5), deposit and
-- advance accounts and Government funds beyond what is paid into them (ss 8 to 10, 13, 14), refunds (s 16), the estimates and
-- personnel list (s 17(1) to (3)), the yearly statement of accounts (s 18), write-off (s 19), and regulations (s 24). The Act creates
-- no offence and no penalty; nothing of that kind is encoded because there is none.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Financial Procedure Act 1966 -- controls on public money`

§§ `2 -- the financial year`

-- s 2(1): "'financial year' means a period of 12 months ending on 31 March in any year".
-- (Which year a given month falls in is an inference from that definition; the Act names no financial year by number.)
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year in which that financial year ends` MEANS
    IF `the month` AT MOST 3 THEN `the calendar year` ELSE `the calendar year` PLUS 1

§§ `2A(2) -- the Accountant-General's terms`

-- s 2A(2): "The remuneration and other terms of service of the Accountant-General must not be altered to his or her disadvantage
-- during his or her continuance in office."
GIVEN `still in office` IS A BOOLEAN, `the change is to the Accountant-General's disadvantage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change to the Accountant-General's terms is permitted` IF
    (NOT `still in office`) OR (NOT `the change is to the Accountant-General's disadvantage`)

§§ `4 -- bank accounts and overdrafts`

-- s 4: "No accounting officer shall open any public or official account in respect of public moneys of Singapore in any bank without
-- the authority in writing of the Minister, and no bank shall permit an overdraft on any public or official account ... unless the
-- same be authorised by the Minister or under the authority of any written law."
GIVEN `the Minister authorised it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accounting officer may open the account` IF `the Minister authorised it in writing`

GIVEN `the Minister authorised the overdraft` IS A BOOLEAN, `a written law authorises the overdraft` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bank may permit the overdraft` IF
    `the Minister authorised the overdraft` OR `a written law authorises the overdraft`

§§ `6 -- the two Consolidated Fund accounts`

-- s 6: "(a) ... the Consolidated Revenue Account in which account shall be kept all moneys in the Fund other than such moneys as are
-- mentioned in paragraph (b); (b) ... the Consolidated Loan Account in which account shall be kept all moneys received by way of loan
-- upon the public credit of Singapore and that are not to refinance an earlier borrowing under the Significant Infrastructure
-- Government Loan Act 2021."
-- Read literally, loan money that DOES refinance an earlier SIGLA borrowing falls into (a), the Revenue Account.
DECLARE `Consolidated Fund account` IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Revenue Account`
    `the Consolidated Loan Account`

GIVEN `received by way of loan on the public credit` IS A BOOLEAN, `to refinance an earlier SIGLA borrowing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Consolidated Fund account`
`the account the money is kept in` MEANS
    IF `received by way of loan on the public credit` AND (NOT `to refinance an earlier SIGLA borrowing`)
    THEN `the Consolidated Loan Account`
    ELSE `the Consolidated Revenue Account`

§§ `7 -- investment of public moneys`

-- s 7(3): moneys may be invested by the Minister "(a) on deposit in any bank; (b) in gold and other bullion; (c) in securities of, or
-- guaranteed by, any government or international financial institution; (d) in any of the stocks, funds, securities or investments;
-- or (e) as otherwise authorised by law". (Paragraph (d) is unqualified as deposited.)
-- s 7(4): they "shall not be invested by the Minister in any stock, bond, fund or security issued by the Government of Singapore".
-- s 7(7): "Notwithstanding subsection (3), moneys specified in the Schedule and paid to the credit of any deposit account ... shall be
-- invested by the Minister on deposit in any bank." (The Schedule has no entries in the deposit.)
DECLARE Investment IS ONE OF
    `a deposit in a bank`
    `gold bullion`
    `bonds of a foreign government`
    `bonds of an international financial institution`
    `bonds guaranteed by a foreign government`
    `listed company shares`
    `bonds issued by the Government of Singapore`
    `an investment otherwise authorised by law`

GIVEN `the investment` IS AN Investment, `the moneys are Schedule moneys in a deposit account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may make the investment` IF
    IF `the moneys are Schedule moneys in a deposit account`
    THEN `the investment` EQUALS `a deposit in a bank`
    ELSE NOT (`the investment` EQUALS `bonds issued by the Government of Singapore`)

-- s 7(5): income "shall be accounted in the Consolidated Revenue Account, except that where it is so provided in any law or under the
-- terms of any trust, or the Minister so directs, the interest ... from the investment of any moneys standing to the credit of any
-- trust account shall be paid to the credit of such trust account".
-- s 7(8): interest on Schedule moneys is paid to the deposit account as the Minister directs; "any balance of interest not so paid"
-- goes to the Consolidated Revenue Account.
DECLARE `Income destination` IS ONE OF
    `to the Consolidated Revenue Account`
    `to the trust account`
    `to the deposit account`

GIVEN `from a trust account` IS A BOOLEAN, `a law, the trust terms or the Minister so provides` IS A BOOLEAN, `interest on Schedule moneys the Minister directs to the deposit account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Income destination`
`where the investment income goes` MEANS
    IF `interest on Schedule moneys the Minister directs to the deposit account`
    THEN `to the deposit account`
    ELSE IF `from a trust account` AND `a law, the trust terms or the Minister so provides`
         THEN `to the trust account`
         ELSE `to the Consolidated Revenue Account`

§§ `7A -- capital injections into statutory corporations`

-- s 7A(1): "the Minister may invest by way of capital injection in any statutory corporation out of a capital contribution
-- appropriated by Parliament from the Consolidated Fund by written law". (5): "'statutory corporation' means any body corporate
-- established by or under written law to perform or discharge any public function".
GIVEN `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `established by or under written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `performs a public function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a statutory corporation` IF
    `a body corporate` AND `established by or under written law` AND `performs a public function`

GIVEN `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `established by or under written law` IS A BOOLEAN, `performs a public function` IS A BOOLEAN, `out of a capital contribution appropriated by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may make the capital injection` IF
    `it is a statutory corporation` `a body corporate` `established by or under written law` `performs a public function`
    AND `out of a capital contribution appropriated by written law`

§§ `11 -- Contingencies Fund advances`

-- s 11(2): the Minister may advance from the Contingencies Fund "if he or she is satisfied that there has arisen an urgent and
-- unforeseen need for expenditure for which no other provision exists and for which funds cannot be provided under section 17(4) and
-- if the President, acting in his or her discretion, concurs".
-- Section 17(4) is virement within a head: the Contingencies Fund is the fallback after virement fails.
GIVEN `urgent` IS A BOOLEAN, `unforeseen` IS A BOOLEAN, `no other provision exists` IS A BOOLEAN, `virement under s 17(4) could cover it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President concurs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may advance from the Contingencies Fund` IF
    `urgent` AND `unforeseen` AND `no other provision exists` AND (NOT `virement under s 17(4) could cover it`) AND `the President concurs`

§§ `12(3) -- warrants for expenditure from the Consolidated Fund`

-- s 12(3)(a): the Minister may by warrant authorise issue to meet expenditure "(i) appropriated by a Supply or Supplementary Supply law
-- or any other law or approved by resolution of Parliament in accordance with Article 148A(2) ...; or (ii) approved by resolution of
-- Parliament in accordance with Article 148B(1) ... with which the President concurs: Provided that the aggregate of such sums under
-- each head of expenditure shall not exceed the total sum so approved."
-- (b): also "(i) approved by resolution of Parliament in accordance with Article 148B(2) ... with which the President concurs; or
-- (ii) approved by the Cabinet in accordance with Article 148B(4)". The aggregate-cap proviso is attached to (a) only.
DECLARE `Basis for issue` IS ONE OF
    `a Supply law`
    `a resolution under Article 148A(2)`
    `a resolution under Article 148B(1)`
    `a resolution under Article 148B(2)`
    `Cabinet approval under Article 148B(4)`
    `no approval at all`

GIVEN `already issued under the head` IS A NUMBER, `this issue` IS A NUMBER, `the total approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aggregate stays within the approved total` IF
    `already issued under the head` PLUS `this issue` AT MOST `the total approved`

GIVEN `the basis` IS A `Basis for issue`, `the President concurs` IS A BOOLEAN, `already issued under the head` IS A NUMBER, `this issue` IS A NUMBER, `the total approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may issue by warrant` IF
    CONSIDER `the basis`
    WHEN `a Supply law` THEN `the aggregate stays within the approved total` `already issued under the head` `this issue` `the total approved`
    WHEN `a resolution under Article 148A(2)` THEN `the aggregate stays within the approved total` `already issued under the head` `this issue` `the total approved`
    WHEN `a resolution under Article 148B(1)` THEN `the President concurs` AND `the aggregate stays within the approved total` `already issued under the head` `this issue` `the total approved`
    WHEN `a resolution under Article 148B(2)` THEN `the President concurs`
    WHEN `Cabinet approval under Article 148B(4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no approval at all` THEN FALSE

§§ `15 -- guarantees and loans`

-- s 15(1): "No guarantee involving a financial liability shall be binding upon Singapore unless given with the written authority of
-- the Minister with which the President concurs or in accordance with law."
-- (2): "No loan raised by the Government shall be binding upon Singapore unless it is raised in accordance with Article 144".
GIVEN `the Minister gave written authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the President concurs` IS A BOOLEAN, `given in accordance with law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the guarantee binds Singapore` IF
    (`the Minister gave written authority` AND `the President concurs`) OR `given in accordance with law`

GIVEN `raised in accordance with Article 144` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan binds Singapore` IF `raised in accordance with Article 144`

§§ `17(4) -- virement between subheads`

-- s 17(4): "If the exigencies of the public service render it necessary to alter the proportions assigned to the subheads under a head
-- ... or to create a new subhead, the Minister may by warrant authorise the transfer of a further sum out of any surplus arising on any
-- other subhead of the same head, in aid of any subhead which may be deficient, ... or any new subhead."
-- (That the transfer cannot exceed the surplus is an inference from "out of any surplus".)
GIVEN `the exigencies require it` IS A BOOLEAN, `by warrant` IS A BOOLEAN, `from a subhead of the same head` IS A BOOLEAN, `the amount` IS A NUMBER, `the surplus on the source subhead` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the virement is authorised` IF
    `the exigencies require it` AND `by warrant` AND `from a subhead of the same head` AND `the amount` AT MOST `the surplus on the source subhead`

§§ `17A -- transfer of functions between heads`

-- s 17A(1): where responsibility for a service moves to another head after the Supply law, the Minister "may in writing direct that
-- the appropriation shall not lapse but may be issued to, or applied by, that other head". (2): "a copy of the direction [must be]
-- laid before Parliament within 30 days after it is given."
GIVEN `days after the direction was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction was laid in time` IF `days after the direction was given` AT MOST 30

§§ `20 to 23 -- surcharge`

-- s 20(1): if it appears to the Minister that a person "who is or was in the employment of the Government" (a) failed to collect moneys
-- owing that he or she was responsible for collecting; (b) is or was responsible for an improper payment, or a payment "not duly
-- vouched"; or (c) is or was responsible for a deficiency in, or destruction of, public moneys, stamps, securities, stores or other
-- Government property, "and if a satisfactory explanation is not, within a period specified by the Minister, furnished", the Minister
-- may refer the matter to the appropriate Service Commission, which may "surcharge against that person the whole or such proportion as
-- it thinks fit" of the amount, or "the original value of the property destroyed".
-- (2): "the appropriate Service Commission" means the Public Service Commission, the Judicial Service Commission or the Legal Service
-- Commission.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `failure to collect moneys owing`
    `an improper payment`
    `a payment not duly vouched`
    `a deficiency in public moneys or property`
    `destruction of Government property`
    `a bad but proper policy decision`

DECLARE Commission IS ONE OF
    `the Public Service Commission`
    `the Judicial Service Commission`
    `the Legal Service Commission`
    `the Accountant-General`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Commission
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an appropriate Service Commission` IF
    NOT (`the body` EQUALS `the Accountant-General`)

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a ground for surcharge` IF
    NOT (`the ground` EQUALS `a bad but proper policy decision`)

DECLARE `Surcharge matter`
    HAS `is or was a Government employee` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the ground` IS A Ground
        `gave a satisfactory explanation in time` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the Minister referred it` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the body` IS A Commission
        `the amount at stake` IS A NUMBER
        `the surcharge` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Surcharge matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surcharge may be made` IF
        `the matter`'s `is or was a Government employee`
    AND `it is a ground for surcharge` (`the matter`'s `the ground`)
    AND (NOT `the matter`'s `gave a satisfactory explanation in time`)
    AND `the matter`'s `the Minister referred it`
    AND `it is an appropriate Service Commission` (`the matter`'s `the body`)
    AND `the matter`'s `the surcharge` AT MOST `the matter`'s `the amount at stake`

-- s 22: the Commission "may at any time withdraw any surcharge in respect of which a satisfactory explanation has been received or if it
-- otherwise appears that no surcharge should have been made".
GIVEN `a satisfactory explanation has since been received` IS A BOOLEAN, `it appears no surcharge should have been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may withdraw the surcharge` IF
    `a satisfactory explanation has since been received` OR `it appears no surcharge should have been made`

-- s 23: a surcharge "not withdrawn under section 22 shall be a debt due to the Government"; the Minister may direct recovery "by equal
-- monthly instalments by deductions from the salary or pension ... in amounts not exceeding one-fourth of the total monthly salary or
-- pension".
GIVEN `the surcharge was made` IS A BOOLEAN, `the surcharge was withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the surcharge is a debt due to the Government` IF
    `the surcharge was made` AND (NOT `the surcharge was withdrawn`)

GIVEN `the monthly salary or pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest monthly deduction` MEANS `the monthly salary or pension` DIVIDED BY 4

GIVEN `the deduction` IS A NUMBER, `the monthly salary or pension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction is within the limit` IF
    `the deduction` AT MOST `the largest monthly deduction` `the monthly salary or pension`
